# Origin (Patternflow port)

Concentric sine waves sampled on an emergent tile grid. Port of Seunghun
LEE's Patternflow pattern (CC-BY-SA-4.0).

**Input:** move the mouse over the canvas. Hold **Shift** for the other pair.

| | no Shift | Shift |
|--|----------|-------|
| X | hue | mode / tiling (0..4) |
| Y | speed | frequency |

Knobs only change while the pointer is moving (same sticky rule as the
hardware encoders). Drawing uses `drawRect` for each lit grid cell — no
`setPixel`. Click the canvas after Run.

## Schema

```
Layout = Int/rows Int/cols Int/gap Int/tileSize Int/gridStep Int/gridCells
Cell = Int/x Int/y Int/size Int/rgb
Params = Float/hue Float/speed Float/mode Float/freq Float/time Float/lastX Float/lastY
>Pointer = Float/x Float/y Bool/shift
Game = Params $Pointer @WCHNTMaths/maths Int/w Int/h
```

## Construction

```
[:Game
  [:Params 0.0 2.0 0.0 0.06 0.0 -1.0 -1.0]
  [:Pointer 0.5 0.5 false]
  maths
  800
  600
]
```

## Methods

```
Pointer::update! = { [:Pointer x y shift] }

Game::layout = {
  m = maths.floor(params.mode).
  switch (m)
    0 -> { [:Layout 1 2 4 56 7 8] }
    1 -> { [:Layout 2 4 3 27 3 9] }
    2 -> { [:Layout 3 6 2 18 3 6] }
    3 -> { [:Layout 3 6 2 18 2 9] }
    else -> { [:Layout 6 12 0 10 2 5] }
}

Game::shade = {
  Float/tt, Float/hue |
  if (tt >= 0.816) { 16777215 }
  (tt >= 0.556) { maths.hsv(hue, 1.0, 1.5) }
  (tt >= 0.154) { 657930 }
  else { 0 }
}

Game::cellAt = {
  Int/i, Layout/lay |
  gc = lay.gridCells.
  gx = i % gc.
  gy = (i / gc) % gc.
  ti = ((i / gc) / gc) % lay.cols.
  tj = ((i / gc) / gc) / lay.cols.
  cellW = lay.tileSize + lay.gap.
  cellH = lay.tileSize + lay.gap.
  totalW = (lay.cols * lay.tileSize) + ((lay.cols + 1) * lay.gap).
  totalH = (lay.rows * lay.tileSize) + ((lay.rows + 1) * lay.gap).
  offsetX = (w - totalW) / 2.
  offsetY = (h - totalH) / 2.
  half = lay.gridStep / 2.
  sx = (gx * lay.gridStep) + half.
  sy = (gy * lay.gridStep) + half.
  cx = lay.tileSize / 2.
  dx = sx - cx.
  dy = sy - cx.
  dist = maths.sqrt((dx * dx) + (dy * dy)).
  knobFreqBase = 50.0 + (params.freq * 950.0).
  knobFreqVar = params.freq * 1000.0.
  tileFreq = knobFreqBase + (((tj * lay.cols) + ti) * (knobFreqVar * 0.15)).
  wave = maths.sin((dist * (tileFreq * 0.5)) + (params.time * 2.0)).
  tt = maths.min(1.0, maths.max(0.0, ((wave * 0.8) + 1.0) * 0.5)).
  rgb = this.shade(tt, params.hue).
  px = (offsetX + lay.gap) + (ti * cellW) + (gx * lay.gridStep).
  py = (offsetY + lay.gap) + (tj * cellH) + (gy * lay.gridStep).
  [:Cell px py lay.gridStep rgb]
}

Game::cells = {
  lay = this.layout().
  n = ((((lay.rows * lay.cols) * lay.gridCells) * lay.gridCells)).
  n.times({ i | this.cellAt(i, lay) }).filter({ Cell/c | c.rgb > 0 })
}

Game::draw = { @WCHNTGraphics/g |
  this.cells().fold(g.background(0x000000).clear().noStroke(), { @WCHNTGraphics/acc, Cell/c |
    acc.beginFill(c.rgb).drawRect(c.x, c.y, c.size, c.size).endFill()
  })
}

Game::update! = {
  movedX = maths.abs(pointer.x - params.lastX) > 0.000001.
  movedY = maths.abs(pointer.y - params.lastY) > 0.000001.
  hue = if ((not pointer.shift) and movedX) { pointer.x } else { params.hue }.
  speed = if ((not pointer.shift) and movedY) { pointer.y * 4.0 } else { params.speed }.
  mode = if (pointer.shift and movedX) { pointer.x * 4.0 } else { params.mode }.
  freq = if (pointer.shift and movedY) { pointer.y } else { params.freq }.
  nt = params.time + (0.016 * speed).
  [:Game [:Params hue speed mode freq nt pointer.x pointer.y] pointer maths w h]
}
```

## Target

```
%canvas

%requires
WCHNTMaths::sin(Float) -> Float
WCHNTMaths::sqrt(Float) -> Float
WCHNTMaths::abs(Float) -> Float
WCHNTMaths::floor(Float) -> Int
WCHNTMaths::hsv(Float, Float, Float) -> Int
WCHNTMaths::max(Float, Float) -> Float
WCHNTMaths::min(Float, Float) -> Float

%init
var assemblage;

function init() {
    assemblage = GameAssemblage.factory(wchntMaths);
}

%step
function step() {
    var m = input.mouse;
    assemblage.pointer.inject(m.x, m.y, !!input.keys.Shift);
    assemblage.draw(wchntGraphics);
}
```
